        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: What Dreams May Come, Hamlet, \"To be, or not to be\"\n- People: Richard Matheson, William Shakespeare, Prince Hamlet\n- Concepts: titles, soliloquies, literary quotations\n\nFacts:\n- William Shakespeare wrote the play Hamlet, which includes the soliloquy that begins with the phrase \"To be, or not to be\".\n- Prince Hamlet speaks the \"To be, or not to be\" soliloquy in the so-called nunnery scene of Hamlet.\n- Richard Matheson's 1983 novel What Dreams May Come derives its title from a line in Hamlet's \"To be, or not to be\" soliloquy.",
